# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# `docker compose build` uses ./backend as its context, and the Dockerfile ends
# with `COPY . .`. Everything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon on every
# build and baked into the image.
#
# Added in D01, when `backend/venv` was created: a local virtualenv holding torch,
# ultralytics and mediapipe is several gigabytes, and without this file every build
# spends minutes uploading it and then bakes a Linux image full of Windows wheels
# that can never be imported.
# =============================================================================

# ---- virtual environments ----------------------------------------------------
# Platform-specific and enormous. The image installs its own dependencies from
# requirements/, and a host venv in the image would be both useless and confusing.
venv/
.venv/
venv.bak/
env/

# ---- Python caches -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# ---- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` is deliberately NOT copied into the image.
#
# docker-compose reads it with `env_file:` on the HOST and injects the values as
# environment variables, so the container still gets everything it needs —
# pydantic-settings reads the environment before it reads a file. Baking the file
# in would put the Supabase service-role key, the JWT secret and the SMTP password
# into an image layer, where they survive even if the file is later deleted.
#
# If the API starts and complains that DATABASE_URL is missing, the cause is
# compose not loading env_file, not this exclusion.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- model weights -----------------------------------------------------------
# Mounted as the `model_cache` volume at runtime, and yolov9c.pt is downloaded in
# its own cached layer by the Dockerfile. Copying host copies in would add ~700 MB
# for no benefit.
*.pt
*.onnx
*.pth
cache/

# ---- runtime output ----------------------------------------------------------
# Bind-mounted by compose, so the image copies are dead weight.
logs/
uploads/
*.log

# ---- local tooling and docs --------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
setup_venv.bat
setup_venv.ps1
